                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> According to the <title>DNB</title>, Thomas Skinner Surr
(1770-1847), novelist,
married Miss Griffiths, sister-in-law 
of <persName key="PHI01">Sir Richard Phillips</persName> (1767–1840). 
Surr (or the Surrs) appears with Philips regularly throughout the diary between 1801 and 1819 and in 1807 Godwin also reads Surr.
At Philips's on 31 Aug 1806 Godwin dines with 'T Moore, Wolcot, Busby, Raymonds, Saxon, 
Magnys, Cooper, Hardy and Surrs; adv.
 Thorntons, Browns, and Batty and Keys'.
There is no mention of Surr in the Godwin biographies.</p>
                    </note>
